# sound: on
# config: mock.json
#
# A placed stone must actually be heard, not merely requested.
#
# "Sometimes there is no sound when I place a stone" had no symptom anything
# could assert on: GobanView logged "Playing stone sound in repaint" either way,
# and whether the mixer ever saw the request was invisible. `sounds_played`
# counts playbacks mixed all the way to their end, incremented by the audio
# callback itself, so this fails if a sound is swallowed rather than played.
#
# The gaps matter. Sounds arriving back to back keep the stream running and hide
# every defect in this path; the one that goes missing is the first after a
# quiet spell, which is exactly the stone a human places after thinking.

new_game 9
wait_idle
switch_player black human
switch_player white human
wait_idle

click 2 2
wait_idle
click 2 2
wait_until move_count >= 1
wait 3000

click 6 6
wait_idle
click 6 6
wait_until move_count >= 2
wait 3000

click 4 4
wait_idle
click 4 4
wait_until move_count >= 3
wait 2000

expect move_count 3
expect sounds_played 3
